Full budgets: `docs/PERFORMANCE.md`. Style: `docs/ART_DIRECTION.md`.

- Renderer: `THREE.WebGLRenderer` (WebGL2), `powerPreference: 'high-performance'`, `antialias: false`
  (AA comes from the post pass per preset). Never set pixel ratio above 1; resolution is controlled by the
  dynamic resolution scaler in `src/render`.
- Every feature reads the active quality preset (`low | medium | high`) and must have a cheap Low path.
- Draw calls: use `InstancedMesh` for repeated props, merge static geometry per world chunk, share
  materials. Check `renderer.info.render.calls` in the perf HUD after every change.
- Overdraw is the main enemy on integrated GPUs: few large transparent surfaces, sort and cap particles,
  no full-screen transparent layers stacked on each other.
- Lighting: one directional sun + hemisphere ambient. No extra dynamic point/spot lights in gameplay; fake
  glow with emissive materials and additive sprites. Shadows only from the sun, only near the camera, map
  size from the preset.
- Materials: `MeshLambertMaterial` or our stylized shader for the world; `MeshStandardMaterial` only for
  dragons and hero props. Compile shaders during loading (`renderer.compileAsync`) so nothing hitches
  mid-match.
- Textures are KTX2 (load with `KTX2Loader`), models are meshopt-compressed GLB (`MeshoptDecoder`). Do
  not load PNG/JPG textures at runtime except UI images.
- No allocations in `update`/`render`: preallocate scratch `Vector3`/`Quaternion`/`Matrix4` at module level.
- Read game state only through the `WorldView` / event contracts in `src/shared`. Never import from
  `src/sim` or `src/net` internals.
- Dispose geometries, materials and textures when leaving a scene (lobby → match → results).
